    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0130" n="114" xml:id="pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.01/11–1048: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Certain Diplomatic Representatives in the American
                            Republics
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d90-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-10">November 10,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dept considering resumption normal diplomatic relations with Peru accordance
                    Resolution 35 Bogotá Conference. Before taking action desires know attitude
                    other Amer Republics which have not yet taken
                    action. Consult FonMin re foregoing and tel
                    any views he may express.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d90-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d90-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Embassies in Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Cuba, Mexico,
                    Nicaragua, Panama, Uruguay, Venezuela, Ecuador, El Salvador, Guatemala, Haiti,
                    Honduras, Paraguay; repeated for information to Embassies in Argentina,
                    Dominican Republic, Peru, and Bolivia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
